-	CGO_ENABLED=0 go build -trimpath -ldflags="$(GO_LDFLAGS)" -o $(GUEST_AGENT) .
-	CGO_ENABLED=0 go build -trimpath -ldflags="$(GO_LDFLAGS)" -o $(PHIALD) ./cmd/phiald
-	CGO_ENABLED=0 go build -trimpath -ldflags="$(GO_LDFLAGS)" -o bin/phial .
-	CGO_ENABLED=0 go build -trimpath -ldflags="$(GO_LDFLAGS)" -o $(PHIALD_BINARY) ./cmd/phiald
-
-guest-agent:
-	CGO_ENABLED=0 go build -trimpath -ldflags="$(GO_LDFLAGS)" -o $(GUEST_AGENT) .
-
-generate:
-	cd assets/resources && blueprint-compiler batch-compile . . *.blp
-	cd assets/resources && glib-compile-schemas .
-	cd assets/resources && glib-compile-resources index.gresource.xml
-
-install: build
-	./bin/phial host-install --config "$(HOME)/.config/phial" --data "$(HOME)/.local/share/phial" --ssh "$(HOME)/.ssh"
-
-test:
-	go test ./...
-
-acceptance: build
-	./bin/phial acceptance
-
-ui-test: generate
-	./tests/ui-test.sh
-
-wizard-test: generate
-	./tests/wizard-test.sh
-
-pot:
-	cd po && go generate ./...
-
-flatpak-lint:
-	python3 -c "import json; json.load(open('flatpak/com.pojtinger.felicitas.Phial.json')); print('manifest ok')"
-
-flatpak: flatpak-lint
-	flatpak-builder --disable-rofiles-fuse --force-clean --repo=flatpak/repo flatpak/build flatpak/com.pojtinger.felicitas.Phial.json
-	flatpak build-bundle flatpak/repo flatpak/phial.flatpak com.pojtinger.felicitas.Phial
-
-clean:
-	rm -rf bin/phial $(PHIALD_BINARY) $(GUEST_AGENT) $(PHIALD) flatpak/build flatpak/repo flatpak/phial.flatpak
diff --git a/README.md b/README.md
deleted file mode 100644
index 6286bcae75dd8fd06239084a4dcab0a69724a31e..0000000000000000000000000000000000000000
--- a/README.md
+++ /dev/null
@@ -1,176 +0,0 @@
-# Phial
-
-Run development machines with time-boxed access to your secrets.
-
-![The machine page](assets/meta/screenshot-machine.png)
-
-## Overview
-
-Phial runs Fedora virtual machines on your desktop. Every secret and every private
-key stays on the host. A machine receives access to one secret or one key, for one
-machine, for a set time, and nothing more.
-
-The host is trusted. The machine is not trusted. Read [docs/DESIGN.md](docs/DESIGN.md)
-for the interface design, the gate design, and the threat model.
-
-## Terms
-
-- A machine is one Fedora guest with its own disk, memory, and device list.
-- A secret is a value in the keyring of the host, the Secret Service of the session.
-- Env mode means that the machine reads a secret from a file in its own share.
-- Proxy mode means that the host injects a secret into an outbound request.
-- A key lives in the SSH agent of the session or in the GnuPG agent of the host.
-- A grant is a time box or a single use of one secret or key for one machine.
-- A share is a host directory that the machine mounts over virtiofs.
-
-## Install
-
-Install the tools for the host setup:
-
-    sudo dnf install waypipe virt-firmware pinentry-gnome3
-
-Install a client for `rdp://` links, such as Remmina:
-
-    flatpak install flathub org.remmina.Remmina
-
-Set the client as the default handler for `rdp://` links:
-
-    xdg-mime default org.remmina.Remmina.desktop x-scheme-handler/rdp
-
-Build the binary and install the pieces into your user directories:
-
-    make install
-
-Apply the system setup. The application does the same from the System Setup dialog:
-
-    ./bin/phial root-setup
-
-## The application
-
-Start Phial with no argument to open the window:
-
-    phial
-
-The window carries a sidebar. The sidebar lists every machine, then Secrets and
-Grants. Select an entry to show it in the content area.
-
-### Machines
-
-Select a machine in the sidebar to open its page. The page reports the state, the
-live usage, the configuration, the USB devices, the shares, and the access paths.
-
-The header carries one primary control. The control is Install, Start, or Stop,
-depending on the state. The menu next to it carries the machine settings, the SSH
-command, a restart, and the delete control.
-
-Press Install to fetch the Fedora netinst image and to write the system. The page
-then lists every install step and a Cancel Installation control.
-
-### Secrets
-
-The Secrets page lists what a machine can be granted: the SSH keys of your session
-agent, the GnuPG keys of the host, and the secrets of the host keyring. Add a key
-from a file, generate a new one, or store a secret. The private parts never leave
-the host. Grant an entry to a machine from its row.
-
-### Grants
-
-A grant opens one secret or key for one machine: time-boxed, one use, or until
-revoked. The Grants page lists every open grant with its machine and its remaining
-time. Revoke a grant from its row.
-
-An agent inside a machine can ask the host for a grant, or to store or remove a
-secret or a key. Every request waits on the Grants page. Approve or deny each
-request. A request that nobody answers within five minutes counts as denied.
-
-The gate on the host enforces every grant. The machine reaches the SSH agent, the
-GnuPG agent, and the proxy through it. Before the gate signs with a key, it asks
-you with a prompt on the host.
-
-### System Setup
-
-The main menu carries System Setup. The dialog reports the host requirements and
-applies the root setup through polkit. The About dialog carries the acceptance
-report as debug information.
-
-## The agent channel
-
-Phial serves a Model Context Protocol endpoint on two sockets:
-
-- `$XDG_RUNTIME_DIR/phial/mcp.sock` serves the host.
-- `$XDG_RUNTIME_DIR/phial/mcp-guest.sock` serves the machine.
-
-The machine reaches the host endpoint through vsock port 8080 at
-`http://host.internal:8080/mcp`. The host knows which machine a request comes
-from by the vsock address of the connection. List the tools with the
-`tools/list` request. Every control in the window has a matching tool.
-
-## The command line
-
-    phial                     open the window, also serve the agent channel
-    phial --background        start in the background, for autostart
-    phial vm exec <name>      run one machine in the foreground
-    phial vfio <bind|restore> <address>   bind or restore a PCI controller
-    phial root-setup [ethernet] [memory]  apply the system setup, needs run0
-    phial install [repo]      install the binary and the configuration
-    phial acceptance          run the host acceptance checks
-    phial gate                serve the gate that a machine may reach
-    phial forward-guest <name> forward one socket to the host, machine side
-    phial run <command...>    run a command with the granted secrets, machine side
-    phial allow (--for <duration> | --once | --until-revoked) [--vm <machine>] <target>
-    phial revoke [--vm <machine>] <id or target>
-    phial status              show the grants
-    phial ls                  list the secret and key names, never the values
-
-A target is a secret name, `agent://<comment>` for an SSH key of the session, or
-`gpg-agent://` for the GnuPG agent of the host.
-
-## Development
-
-Build the resources and the binary:
-
-    make generate
-    make build
-
-Run the application from the tree:
-
-    GSETTINGS_SCHEMA_DIR=$PWD/assets/resources ./bin/phial
-
-A development build also needs the settings schema on `GSETTINGS_SCHEMA_DIR` and
-the translations on the `main.LocaleDir` link flag. Read the Makefile.
-
-## Testing
-
-Run the unit tests of the engine:
-
-    make test
-
-Run the interface test. It drives the window through its own actions and writes one
-screenshot per page into `/tmp/phial-ui`:
-
-    make ui-test
-
-The test renders the window with the GTK snapshot API. Set `OUT` to write the
-screenshots somewhere else. Set `MACHINE` and `PROVIDER` to name an existing
-machine and provider.
-
-## Flatpak
-
-The manifest sits at flatpak/com.pojtinger.felicitas.Phial.json. It builds
-waypipe, the OVMF firmware pair, and Phial itself from source. Run
-`make flatpak`. Read
-[flatpak/README.md](flatpak/README.md) for the module list and the
-permissions. QEMU runs on the host.
-
-## Translations
-
-The interface strings live in the source. Extract the catalogue and compile the
-translations:
-
-    make pot
-
-## License
-
-Phial (c) 2026 Felicitas Pojtinger and contributors
-
-SPDX-License-Identifier: AGPL-3.0-or-later
